docs/agent-context/codex-loop-context-management.md:19:The strongest transferable idea for Symphony is not Codex global hooks. Symphony already owns the agent launch harness, Agent Worktrees, Runtime State, and Agent Prompt composition. The transferable idea is a bounded, deterministic context snapshot that is generated by the harness immediately before launching or retrying an agent.
docs/agent-context/codex-loop-context-management.md:84:Symphony should not copy `codex-loop`'s global Codex hook installation as the primary design. Codex hooks are useful for a single interactive Codex session. Symphony is already the harness that dispatches agents into Agent Worktrees, writes the prompt, captures stdout/stderr, controls retry, and owns Runtime State.
